comments:
Thanks for tracking it down. So to keep `--pipe` as unintrusive as possible (whereas `--pty` allocates a new PTY and service can do whatever to it), this might help:

```diff
--- a/src/core/exec-invoke.c
+++ b/src/core/exec-invoke.c
@@ -390,8 +390,9 @@ static int setup_input(
                 if (dup2(params->stdin_fd, STDIN_FILENO) < 0)
                         return -errno;
 
-                /* Try to make this the controlling tty, if it is a tty, and reset it */
-                if (isatty(STDIN_FILENO)) {
+                /* Try to make this the controlling tty, if it is a tty, and reset it
+                 * but don't touch tty if it was passed via systemd-run --pipe */
+                if (isatty(STDIN_FILENO) && !context->stdio_as_fds) {
                         unsigned rows = context->tty_rows, cols = context->tty_cols;
 
                         (void) exec_context_tty_size(context, &rows, &cols);
```

But [machine-dbus.c](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/7e472fc9847f921133ecdfc96cd7a7b640cfb9cc/src/machine/machine-dbus.c#L707) would need adjustment to rely only on TTYPath=. There is also TTYReset= but that may not be apply to `setup_input()`.
